────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Third-party components

Tyche depends on TimesFM. Two different licences apply to it and the
distinction matters if this project ever stops being private:

  • The `timesfm` package source is Apache-2.0.
  • The `google/timesfm-3.0-pytorch` *weights* Tyche downloads at runtime are
    distributed under `timesfm-non-commercial-license-v1.0` and are
    restricted to non-commercial, non-production use. Commercial or
    production use of those weights is not permitted.

Weights up to TimesFM 2.5 remain Apache-2.0, so a commercial build would have
to drop to 2.5 — which cannot do native multivariate forecasting and is not a
drop-in swap for what core/forecaster.py does.

CustomTkinter is MIT. NumPy is BSD-3-Clause. Requests is Apache-2.0.
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Draw data

Historical draw results are facts, not creative works. The archive files Tyche
downloads are third-party compilations and each carries its own terms of use;
check them before redistributing a copy of the archive itself.
